hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24086","Narrated to us Yazid, informed to us Ibrahim ibn Saad, informed to me my father, he said: I was sitting beside Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman in the mosque, when a handsome old man of Banu Ghifar passed, and in his ears was deafness, or he said: heaviness. Humayd sent to him. When he came, he said: O nephew, make room for him between me and you, for he accompanied the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he came until he sat between me and him. So Humayd said to him: This hadith which you narrated to me from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the old man said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, creates the clouds, and they speak the best speech, and laugh the best laugh."
"24087","Narrated to us Rawh, narrated to us al-Awzai, from Abdullah ibn Saad, from al-Sunabihi, from a man of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade Ghulutat. al-Awzai said: Ghulutat are severe and difficult questions."
"24088","Narrated to us Ali ibn Bahr, narrated to us Isa ibn Yunus, narrated to us al-Awzai, from Abdullah ibn Saad, from al-Sunabihi, from Muawiyah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade Ghulutat."
